-- Employment Insurance Act (S.C. 1996, c. 23), Schedule V (subsection 12(2.3)): the Table of Weeks of Benefits for Seasonal
-- Workers. Written by piece ei6 (Sonnet 5.5) on 2026-10-24; the rows below were generated by a script that reads the raw file
-- (src:3500-3540), so no figure is typed by hand. Text: the unofficial plain-text rendering of the Justice Laws
-- consolidation current to 2026-09-30; nothing here is claimed to be verified against the official text.
--
-- What the table decides: the maximum number of weeks of regular benefits for a claimant who meets the conditions of
-- s 12(2.3) (a benefit period established from September 26, 2021 to October 7, 2028, a claimant ordinarily resident in a
-- region of Schedule VI, and so on: piece ei1), by hours of insurable employment (the rows) and the regional rate of
-- unemployment (the columns). Whether s 12(2.3) applies is ei1's; here only the table is encoded.
--
-- The same three readings as Schedule I (fork F-ei6-8 in NOTES.md): a blank cell is NOTHING; fewer than 420 hours has no row;
-- a count of hours between two rows (454.5) belongs to the lower row.

§ `Schedule V - Table of Weeks of Benefits - Seasonal Workers`

